# Shaked Levy Studio — Design System

## Philosophy
Build digital experiences that create trust before the first conversation. Every element must have a purpose. Calm, confident, timeless. Never loud, trendy, or corporate.

Feel like Apple / Linear / Framer / Stripe in principles — premium, elegant, quiet, crafted, intentional. Not flashy. Not marketing.

## UX
Each section answers **one question only**. Natural scroll flow. No cognitive overload. No unnecessary choices. Effortless interactions.

## Homepage story (locked order)
Hero → Why websites matter → How we think → Who we build for → Portfolio / Experience → CTA. Nothing else.

## Visual language
Minimalism and aggressive whitespace. Restraint, not decoration. Typography is the hero — large headlines, short paragraphs, obvious hierarchy.

## Colors (never add new ones)
- Primary: white · Secondary: very light gray · Text: near black · Accent: existing accent/brand tokens only
- No colorful gradients. No saturated UI. Use `story-purple`, `accent`, `text`, `secondary` from Tailwind config.

## Surfaces
- Borders: soft, thin — `border-black/[0.05]`–`/[0.07]`
- Shadows: almost invisible, large blur, low opacity — `shadow-depth-*`
- Avoid cards unless necessary; prefer whitespace. If cards: large radius, subtle border/shadow.

## Icons & buttons
Icons: small, monochrome, supportive — never decorative. Buttons: simple, confident spacing; premium hover, not playful.

## Motion
Motion communicates, never entertains. Scroll animations: fade, translate, opacity, small scale only. Duration 500–700ms, stagger 80–150ms. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Browser mockups
Premium macOS window: rounded corners, soft shadow, minimal toolbar, perfect proportions, no fake UI clutter.

## Copy
Human, short, confident. No clichés, buzzwords, or agency language. Never: "stunning experiences" / "next level."

## Conversion
Trust first, lead second. CTAs feel like the natural next step — never pressure.

## Before every change, ask
Does this improve trust, clarity, or conversion? If not — do not implement.

## Never (locked)
Redesign unrelated sections · invent new styles/colors · inconsistent spacing · change typography hierarchy · replace components without instruction · decorative elements · excessive gradients · glassmorphism (unless established) · unnecessary icons · visual noise

## Quality checklist
Visual consistency · typography hierarchy · spacing rhythm · subtle purposeful motion · existing design system · concise copy · one story per section · increases trust · supports conversion · feels handcrafted
